# Direct dependencies for the sensor service.
#
# This file is the INPUT. The lockfile is requirements.txt, generated by:
#
#     uv pip compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# or, for every service at once, `make lock` from the repository root.
#
# Only the identity service used to have this split. Everywhere else the
# transitive tree was resolved fresh at each image build, so two builds of the
# same commit installed different code and the resolver was free to pick
# versions nobody had reviewed -- which is how a 2014 ecdsa release ended up on
# the token-verification path (WILDBO-DEP-02/DEP-04/DEP-05).

# What the sensor imports when it runs, and nothing else: the lock made from
# this file is what the image installs, and setup.py's install_requires. The
# test runner and the linters were here too (pytest, pytest-asyncio,
# pytest-cov, black, flake8, mypy), so the image shipped them and their
# dependencies, and `pip install .` required them (#777). The unit-test job
# installs its own, at the versions of tests/ci-tools/requirements.in, on top
# of this lock (.github/workflows/test.yml); the Code Quality job installs the
# linters from that lock. To run the tests by hand, see the README.
#
# aiohttp-cors went with the CORS layer of the local API (#777).

aiohttp==3.14.3
PyYAML==6.0.2
psutil==6.1.1
cryptography==50.0.2
